            {
                "entry_id": "7275228a-306b-390a-a2ab-c1fd97223135",
                "word": "gilder",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "07f54908-ebed-4243-8185-64ef5568f6f8",
                        "entry_id": "7275228a-306b-390a-a2ab-c1fd97223135",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "gilders"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                        "entry_id": "7275228a-306b-390a-a2ab-c1fd97223135",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative spelling of guilder."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative",
                            "archaic",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4c06b1c-899e-4a01-9049-d81f03ce2c95",
                                "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                                "text": "The enmity and diſcord which of late / Sprung from the rancorous outrage of your Duke, / To Merchants our well-dealing Countrimen, / Who wanting gilders to redeeme their liues, / Haue ſeal'd his rigorous ſtatutes with their blouds, / Excludes all pitty from our threatning lookes: [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bc361ffb-97da-43b4-b528-8050f1c605ec",
                                "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                                "text": "[N]one ſhall be choſen to be a Commiſſioner in the Court at Amſterdam, vnleſſe he put ſix thouſand gilders ſtocke of his owne in the ſaid Companie; [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "011cc233-e3bb-45b0-8452-4148dbcc35d7",
                                "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                                "text": "On the Spuy is a good Dutch Inn, called the Hoff van Utrecht. The Price is a Gilder a Day, or a Shilling for the Dinner only."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0e24f93-e661-450d-822d-cbbcdc564e41",
                                "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                                "text": "In order to restrain excessive and inconsiderate liberality, it was introduced by the written laws, that no present exceeding the amount of five hundred gold gilders of Rome may exist, unless it be made and confirmed publicly and lawfully in writing before the court of justice of the place; [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea578d95-c730-41d0-915a-83310b155d9b",
                                "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                                "text": "On both sides they will confuse you by explaining that the Dutch gilder is the currency they prefer—a type of coin you are certain to be without."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "24df491f-06d0-4844-807f-d49df2694a1e",
                                "sense_id": "c9c8656d-4f97-3e17-ac3d-56578b403c00",
                                "text": "[...] i.e. the 11 'legacy' currencies replaced by the euro on 1 January 1999 (Portuguese escudo, Belgian and Luxembourg franc, French franc, Dutch gilder, Italian lira, [...])."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
